# Frontend conventions

## Copy by page kind

- **Simple list CRUD** (settings-style table + modal): `containers/setting/UnitsPage/` + `api/hooks/unit/` + `api/requests/units.ts`
- **Complex create / multi-section form**: `containers/order/CreateOrderPage/` (items table, client, payments; shared bits in `order/components/`)
- **Warehouse receive / document flow**: `containers/warehouseTransaction/WarehouseTransactionReceivePage/`
- **Money transactions** (list + richer create form): `containers/MoneyTransactionsPage/`

Same shell for all: `index.tsx` (layout) + `context.tsx` (state/mutations) + `components/`.

## Structure

- `app/App.tsx` — routes + `ProtectedRoute` (`entity.page`)
- `containers/.../<X>Page/index.tsx` — shell only (Helmet + Provider + sections)
- `context.tsx` — forms, mutations, toasts, invalidation — not raw `fetch`
- Page `components/` — UI for this page; cross-page pieces for one domain live next to siblings (e.g. `order/components/`)
- `components/` + `components/ui/` — shared UI / primitives
- `api/requests/` — HTTP; `api/hooks/<entity>/` — React Query
- `locales/en` + `locales/ru` — all user-visible strings

## MUST / NEVER

- MUST: wire page through context + hooks; presentational components stay dumb
- MUST: gate actions with `PermissionGate` — **same** string as backend route
- MUST: locale keys for each language
- NEVER: put HTTP/business rules in page components when context exists
- NEVER: copy UnitsPage patterns onto multi-step create docs — use CreateOrder / Receive / MoneyTransactions as above
- Money: UI may show major; API payloads stay minor
